{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1017679-how-does-countermagick-works-systemwise","id":1017679,"title":"How does Countermagick works, systemwise","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-15T09:17:32-08:00","id":1017679,"title":"How does Countermagick works, systemwise","content":"i seen that some characters have the &quot;Countermagick&quot; stat, but i never was able to figure out how exactly does it work, can someone try to explain it to me please?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T10:33:29-08:00","id":1017706,"title":"","content":"Countermagick is something like a magical dodge, block or parry.<br /> As long as you have an action/dice left you can utter a counterspell/use your X-17b\u2122 Cancellationtransmitter/etc.<br /> Normally Countermagick is based on Arete/Enlightenment. There are other sources(Familiars, Primium, Wonders, Hedge Magic, Bygone Special Advantages).<br /> <br /> You roll your dice (difficulty is 7, most of the time).<br /> Each success of yours cancels one of the Attacker's. If you bring their successes below the goal of their effect then you have countered it. Otherwise it goes off, but weakened.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T13:17:19-08:00","id":1017770,"title":"","content":"The Countermagic stat itself (as generated by things such as Primium and opposed to the Countermagic action) is rolled vs Magical Effect at Diff 7. Each success removes a success from the Casters roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T17:41:40-08:00","id":1017876,"title":"","content":"is countermagick vulgar or is it coincidential?..or depends on the PC?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T18:10:58-08:00","id":1017884,"title":"","content":"The way I've usually done Counter spells is like this:<br /> <br /> 1. Must have the relevant spheres involved. (all of them)<br /> 2. Must pass a Perception + Awareness roll, or have Prime 1's &quot;Watch the Weaving&quot; effect active in order to know an effect is happening.<br /> 3. Both people roll arete, Successes cancel each other out, and they'll just keep rolling until the caster sets off the effect, or the effect fails.<br /> <br /> If the counterer rolls more successes than caster, they can choose to push the effect back onto them.<br /> If the counterer botches, all the successes they took off are returned.<br /> <br /> The effect always belongs to the caster, it holds their resonance and their the ones who receive paradox for it.<br /> The counterer does not receive paradox for counterspells, if anything they are aiding reality by preventing magic from twisting it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now, as for countermagic as a stat, I am not all that familiar with it, but I don't see why it can't be used in the same way as I've described above.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}